// A read of a variable whose value isn't used compiles to nothing, for the
// global `a`, the block's local `b` (r0) and the captured `c` (r1) alike. The
// discarded lambda is still made with `Closure`, which captures `c`.
// compile: analysed
let a = 1; a; { let b = 2; b; let c = 3; c; fn() { c }; }
